BEFORE PUBLISHING ON apps.odoo.com: replace everything above with the VERBATIM
OPL-1 text from the URL above. This file is a pointer, not the licence. The
manifest's `license: "OPL-1"` is what Odoo reads and is already correct; this
file exists so a human reading the source is not left guessing.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The OASIS base module (oasis_connector) is deliberately LGPL-3 instead: it
carries no business logic, only the app menu, the settings shell and the OASIS
connection settings, so it can be redistributed freely as an install hook.
Depending on LGPL-3 modules (oasis_connector, and Odoo Community's own stock
and purchase) from a proprietary module is permitted — that is precisely what
LGPL allows and AGPL would not.

